# tally 2.2.1 P50 N1: the replaced statement is the last with a row, also behind a `= none` (review
# g4 s223/chain_none_row_nocov). Before W13: loads.
=== options exit=1
=== chain_none_row_nocov.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-04-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-06-30

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2025-01-01..
place sav: accounts PLN lives 2025-01-01..
place shop: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input bank: observed

version open
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  opening[konto] = 1 000.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"
  opening[sav] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"

version stmt
  cite s
  governs 2026-02
  known 2026-03-01
  covers konto
  bank[r1] = (on: 2026-02-10, kind: transfers, leg cash from konto to shop amount 50.00 PLN) "a"
  bank[r2] = (on: 2026-02-11, kind: transfers, leg cash from konto to sav amount 20.00 PLN) "b"

version fix
  cite s
  governs 2026-02
  known 2026-04-01
  replace bank[r1] = none "gone"

version fix3
  cite s
  governs 2026-02
  known 2026-04-10
  replace bank[r1] = (on: 2026-02-10, kind: transfers, leg cash from konto to shop amount 70.00 PLN) "back"

ask q: bal(konto, 2026-04-30), bal(sav, 2026-04-30)
ask q_mid: bal(konto, 2026-04-30) as known 2026-03-15
=== expect
refused: LOAD-COVERS replace bank[r1] of konto: fix3 doesn't cover konto on 2026-02-10 (chain_none_row_nocov.tally:39)
